{
  "dom_id": "step-q172008",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Every integer is either even or odd\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"every\" indicates we should use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to integers. So, by denoting an integer number as $x,$ we have that \n\n$$\n∀\\,x\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as \n\n$$\nx\\text{ is even or }x\\text{ is odd}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows: \n\n$∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x$ is even or $x$ is odd.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
